he bladder, abnormality of vitamin b12 metabolism, acute kidney injury, decreased circulating antibody level, elevated serum creatinine\n  Favours second: autosomal dominant somatic cell mutation, balance problems, bleeding from the gums, blurred vision, cellular immunodeficiency\n\nMyeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Lymphoblastic Lymphoma:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of the bladder, abnormality of vitamin b12 metabolism, acute kidney injury, bone pain, decreased circulating antibody level\n  Favours second: autosomal dominant somatic cell mutation, cellular immunodeficiency, chronic lymphatic leukemia\n\nMyeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Chronic Lymphocytic Leukemia in Blast Crisis:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of the bladder, abnormality of vitamin b12 metabolism, acute kidney injury, decreased circulating antibody level, elevated serum creatinine\n  Favours second: abdominal pain or fullness, anemia, bleeding, easy bruising, fever\n\nChronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm vs De Novo Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (ALL):\n  Favours first:  abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anorexia\n  Favours second: autosomal dominant somatic cell mutation, balance problems, bleeding from the gums, blurred vision, bone pain\n\nChronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm vs Lymphoblastic Lymphoma:\n  Favours first:  abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anorexia\n  Favours second: autosomal dominant somatic cell mutation, cellular immunodeficiency, somatic mutation\n\nChronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm vs Chronic Lymphocytic Leukemia in Blast Crisis:\n  Favours first:  abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anorexia\n  Favours second: abdominal pain or fullness, anemia, bleeding, bone pain, easy bruising\n\nDe Novo Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (ALL) vs Lymphoblastic Lymphoma:\n  Favours first:  balance problems, bleeding from the gums, blurred vision, bone pain, enlarged liver\n\nDe Novo Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (ALL) vs Chronic Lymphocytic Leukemia in Blast Crisis:\n  Favours first:  autosomal dominant somatic cell mutation, balance problems, bleeding from the gums, blurred vision, cellular immunodeficiency\n  Favours second: abdominal pain or fullness, anemia, bleeding, easy bruising, pallor\n\nLymphoblastic Lymphoma vs Chronic Lymphocytic Leukemia in Blast Crisis:\n  Favours first:  autosomal dominant somatic cell mutation, cellular immunodeficiency, chronic lymphatic leukemia, somatic mutation\n  Favours second: abdominal pain or fullness, anemia, bleeding, bone pain, easy bruising\n\nRelated to Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts: cd4+/cd56+ hematodermic neoplasm, hematopoietic and lymphoid cell neoplasm, mast cell neoplasm\n\nRelated to Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm: bone marrow cancer, chronic eosinophilic leukemia, chronic eosinophilic leukemia, not otherwise specified\n\nRelated to De Novo Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (ALL): acute lymphoblastic leukemia (disease), acute lymphoblastic/lymphocytic leukemia, childhood leukemia\n\nRelated to Lymphoblastic Lymphoma: non-hodgkin lymphoma, precursor lymphoblastic lymphoma/leukemia, t-cell childhood lymphoblastic lymphoma\n\n[Indirect reasoning chains (PrimeKG 2-hop):]\n  and night sweats → fatigue → Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts\n  he experienced a headache with blurry vision → seizure → Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm"}
